## General desire lattice

Treat desire as layered rather than as one repeated want. Within the exact
theme requested by the user, combine two or three compatible motives:

- bodily or fluid desire: contact, taste, reception, residue, scent, fullness;
- reproductive desire: insemination, fertilization, pregnancy, visible change;
- marking desire: temporary residue, collar, tattoo, piercing, or other claim;
- function and service: availability, domestic ritual, performance, usefulness;
- degradation or reduction: shame, exposure, animal role, object role, filth;
- modification: training, stretching, conditioning, or permanent alteration;
- destruction and limit fantasy: being pushed, overwhelmed, broken, or spent;
- existential purpose: identity, gratitude, belonging, meaning, or completion.

Only use categories authorized by the scene. A useful combination makes the
same physical beat carry several meanings. For example, reception can also feel
like marking and relationship reassurance; a collar can provide pressure,
audible movement, public evidence, and private relief. Do not turn a request for
one category into an unrelated fetish sampler.

Desire may move through six intensities: curiosity, wanting, needing, craving,
compulsion, and identity. Make escalation observable through choices and
language. Do not jump straight to identity unless current branch evidence or
the user's premise supports it. A fantasy uttered at a peak is not automatically
a permanent character-card fact.
